(The Internal Structure of the Eye) Tj
/F1 12 Tf
16 TL
0 -34 Td
(The human eye is a roughly spherical organ about 24 millimetres across. It) Tj
T*
(works like a camera: a clear front window and an adjustable lens focus light) Tj
T*
(onto a light-sensitive sheet at the back, which converts the image into) Tj
T*
(electrical signals for the brain.) Tj
T*
T*
(The wall of the eyeball is built from three concentric layers, called tunics.) Tj
T*
(The outer fibrous tunic \(sclera and cornea\) gives the eye its shape and) Tj
T*
(protects it. The middle vascular tunic, or uvea \(choroid, ciliary body and) Tj
T*
(iris\), carries blood vessels and controls light and focus. The inner neural) Tj
T*
(tunic is the retina, where vision begins.) Tj
T*
T*
(Inside these layers the eye is divided by the lens into two main segments. The) Tj
T*
(anterior segment in front of the lens is filled with a watery fluid called) Tj
T*
(aqueous humor. The larger posterior segment behind the lens is filled with a) Tj
T*
(clear gel called the vitreous body.) Tj
T*
T*
(Try it: select the paragraph about the three tunics and tap Summarize.) Tj
T*
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
