9 0 obj
<< /Length 1062 >>
stream
BT
/F2 20 Tf
72 720 Td
(The middle layer: the uvea) Tj
/F1 12 Tf
16 TL
0 -34 Td
(The choroid is a thin, dark, highly vascular layer between the sclera and the) Tj
T*
(retina. Its blood vessels nourish the outer part of the retina, including the) Tj
T*
(photoreceptors, and its pigment absorbs stray light so that it does not) Tj
T*
(scatter inside the eye.) Tj
T*
T*
(Toward the front, the choroid thickens into the ciliary body. It contains the) Tj
T*
(ciliary muscle, which is connected to the lens by fine suspensory fibres) Tj
T*
(called zonules. Folds on its inner surface, the ciliary processes, secrete) Tj
T*
(aqueous humor.) Tj
T*
T*
(The iris is the coloured ring at the front of the uvea, with the pupil at its) Tj
T*
(centre. Two smooth muscles control pupil size. The circular sphincter) Tj
T*
(pupillae, supplied by parasympathetic nerves, constricts the pupil in bright) Tj
T*
(light. The radial dilator pupillae, supplied by sympathetic nerves, widens it) Tj
T*
(in dim light. Eye colour depends on the amount of melanin in the iris.) Tj
T*
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
