11 0 obj
<< /Length 1374 >>
stream
BT
/F2 20 Tf
72 720 Td
(Chambers, fluids and the lens) Tj
/F1 12 Tf
16 TL
0 -34 Td
(The space in front of the lens is split by the iris into an anterior chamber) Tj
T*
(\(between cornea and iris\) and a posterior chamber \(between iris and lens\).) Tj
T*
(Aqueous humor is made by the ciliary processes in the posterior chamber, flows) Tj
T*
(through the pupil into the anterior chamber, and drains through the trabecular) Tj
T*
(meshwork into the canal of Schlemm.) Tj
T*
T*
(The balance between production and drainage sets the intraocular pressure,) Tj
T*
(normally about 10 to 21 mmHg. If drainage is impaired the pressure can rise) Tj
T*
(and damage the optic nerve, a condition known as glaucoma.) Tj
T*
T*
(The lens is a transparent, biconvex structure with no blood vessels or nerves,) Tj
T*
(made of tightly packed cells filled with proteins called crystallins. To focus) Tj
T*
(on a near object, the ciliary muscle contracts, the zonules slacken, and the) Tj
T*
(elastic lens becomes rounder. This is called accommodation. With age the lens) Tj
T*
(stiffens \(presbyopia\) and can become cloudy \(cataract\).) Tj
T*
T*
(Behind the lens, the vitreous body fills about 80 percent of the eye's volume.) Tj
T*
(It is roughly 99 percent water held in a mesh of collagen and hyaluronic acid,) Tj
T*
(and it helps keep the retina pressed against the choroid.) Tj
T*
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
