stream
BT
/F2 20 Tf
72 720 Td
(From eye to brain, and quick review) Tj
/F1 12 Tf
16 TL
0 -34 Td
(Each optic nerve runs back to the optic chiasm, where fibres from the nasal) Tj
T*
(half of each retina cross to the other side. The optic tracts carry the) Tj
T*
(signals to the lateral geniculate nucleus of the thalamus, and the optic) Tj
T*
(radiations relay them to the primary visual cortex in the occipital lobe.) Tj
T*
T*
(Quick review. Sclera: white protective coat. Cornea: clear window, most of the) Tj
T*
(focusing power. Choroid: blood supply to the outer retina. Ciliary body: makes) Tj
T*
(aqueous humor and changes lens shape. Iris: controls pupil size. Lens: fine) Tj
T*
(focusing. Vitreous: gel that holds the eye's shape. Retina: converts light) Tj
T*
(into nerve signals. Optic nerve: carries them to the brain.) Tj
T*
T*
(Try it: select the quick review above and tap Flashcards.) Tj
T*
T*
